# The owner's live run of 2026-11-26 (run_win_live.sh live, mode 3), as a
# scripted user: tools/winview --play (its header has the format; screen
# dots of the 640 x 480 view, wall ms).  Motion all the way, at a real
# mouse's rates: every 8 ms (a 125 Hz mouse, or the OS's coalescing at a
# 120 Hz display) or, where a glide ends in 1, every 1 ms (a 1,000 Hz
# mouse with nothing coalescing; the owner's mouse's rate is not known:
# OURS); past the window's edges (SDL reports positions outside the
# window while a button is held); a right double click for the system
# menu, Login PIMOS, the requester's answers typed with the mouse still
# moving, and motion while kl0 runs and draws.  The events the kl0 host
# must recover (moves aside) are run_win_live.sh `flood`'s FLOOD_EXPECT.
glide 600 40 700 1
glide 5 460 600
glide -40 200 300
glide 700 520 300
glide 320 268 500
click r 320 268 70
wait 300
click r 320 268 70
# each pause (600 ms, > the bench's 500 ms quiet) lets kl0 run; the mouse
# moves on while kl0 runs (the bench waits for it) and while its drawing
# goes down the link, contending with the board's answers on the link up
wait 600
glide 200 400 1200 1
glide 600 100 800
glide 489 290 500
wait 100
click l 489 290 80
wait 600
glide 100 100 900 1
glide 600 400 900
glide 300 200 600
drift 500 350 700
type local
key 28
wait 600
glide 100 450 1000 1
glide 600 300 800
drift 200 300 900
type pimos
key 28
wait 600
glide 50 50 1000 1
glide 450 150 800
drift 300 250 500
type Sec
glide 320 240 400
wait 1000
end
